1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,780
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

2
00:00:03,780 --> 00:00:05,720
 Good morning, brothers and sisters.

3
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:09,320
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

4
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:12,160
 Today, we will continue to learn efficiency.

5
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:15,880
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

6
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:19,520
 It's about not just a name, but life.

7
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:22,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:49,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

9
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:53,200
 Therefore, a prisoner for the Lord

10
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:56,640
 urge you to walk in a manner worthy of the calling

11
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,640
 to which you have been called.

12
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:02,240
 With all humility and gentleness,

13
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:05,880
 with patience, bearing with one another in love,

14
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:08,840
 eager to maintain the unity of the spirit

15
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:11,120
 in the bond of peace.

16
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:14,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

17
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:39,680
 There is one body and one spirit,

18
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:42,080
 just as you were called to the one hope that

19
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:43,880
 belonged to your call.

20
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:47,680
 One Lord, one faith, one baptism, one God,

21
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:51,760
 and the Father of all, who is over all, and through all,

22
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:52,800
 and in all.

23
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:55,280
 But grace was given to each one of us

24
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:59,160
 according to the measure of Christ's gift.

25
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:16,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

26
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:20,080
 Before we begin, let me ask you to imagine a scene.

27
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:23,960
 Suppose you walk into the Michelin three-star restaurant.

28
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:29,200
 At the entrance, you see the prestigious Michelin

29
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:31,680
 certification displayed proudly.

30
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:34,800
 The interior is elegant and luxurious.

31
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:37,360
 Every waiter is dressed sharply in suit,

32
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:40,920
 and everything just feels professional.

33
00:02:40,920 --> 00:03:02,760
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

34
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:05,320
 You order their signature pasta dish,

35
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:08,840
 full of anticipation, thinking that today I finally

36
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:12,320
 got the taste of the work of a world-class chef.

37
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:15,720
 A few minutes later, a waiter brings you your food.

38
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:18,280
 You open the plate, and what do you see?

39
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:21,280
 Instant noodle soup in plain hot water

40
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:22,680
 with a sausage on the top.

41
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:23,400
 So you freeze.

42
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:29,440
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

43
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:51,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

44
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:54,120
 You call the manager and ask, wait a minute.

45
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:56,720
 Isn't the Michelin three-star restaurant?

46
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:59,280
 Why are you serving instant noodles?

47
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:02,040
 The manager comes over and calmly says, yes,

48
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:03,840
 we are Michelin three-star.

49
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:05,680
 The certification is real.

50
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:10,160
 As for the food, that's not really the important part.

51
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:12,360
 Would that sound absurd to you?

52
00:04:12,360 --> 00:04:14,440
 Of course it is.

53
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:43,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

54
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:47,680
 And yet, many Christians live exactly like that.

55
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:50,800
 We carry the identity of citizen of heaven.

56
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:53,040
 We carry the label Christian.

57
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:56,080
 We say we belong to God, but our lives often

58
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:58,120
 do not match our identity.

59
00:04:58,120 --> 00:05:01,600
 When conflict comes, we lose our temper immediately.

60
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:05,280
 When interests are threatened, we use worldly method.

61
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:08,600
 We gossip, criticize, and tear others down,

62
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:11,840
 living no differently from the world.

63
00:05:11,840 --> 00:05:34,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

64
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:38,120
 In today's passage, Paul tells us something very important.

65
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:40,440
 Since we are called by God, our lives

66
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:42,480
 should be worthy of that calling.

67
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:45,560
 We should not merely carry a spiritual label

68
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:47,800
 while living in a worldly life.

69
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:50,920
 Today, we will look at this passage in three parts.

70
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:54,880
 First, those who are called must remember their identity.

71
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:57,280
 Second, those who are called must live out

72
00:05:57,280 --> 00:05:59,520
 the character of Christ.

73
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:04,880
 And third, those who are called must diligently preserve unity.

74
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:16,120
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

75
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:38,160
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

76
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:48,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

77
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,560
 Paul says in verse 1, "I, therefore,

78
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:52,880
 a prisoner for the Lord, urge you

79
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:56,200
 to walk in a manner worthy of this calling to which you

80
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,400
 have been called."

81
00:06:57,400 --> 00:07:01,720
 This is a major turning point in the whole book of Ephesians.

82
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:06,840
 What did Paul spend the first three chapters talking about?

83
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:11,800
 He talked about how Father chose us, how Christ redeemed us,

84
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:17,320
 how did the Holy Spirit seal us, and once we were dead in sin.

85
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:19,480
 Well, now we have life.

86
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,040
 And once we were separated from God,

87
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:24,320
 now we belong to God's family.

88
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:27,240
 Only in this chapter 4 does Paul begin

89
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:30,240
 to talk about how should we live.

90
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:58,800
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

91
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:01,080
 This is the logic of our gospel.

92
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:02,480
 Grace comes first.

93
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:04,400
 Response comes second.

94
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,760
 Identity comes first.

95
00:08:05,760 --> 00:08:07,640
 Lifestyle comes second.

96
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:09,480
 God always acts first.

97
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:11,000
 And then we respond.

98
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,400
 God moves first, and then we follow.

99
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:16,320
 This is the gospel.

100
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:42,400
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

101
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:46,320
 Now compare what other religions in the world says.

102
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:47,720
 What do they say?

103
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:49,880
 They will say, fix yourself first.

104
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:53,200
 You have to do your part better first.

105
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:55,040
 And change yourself first.

106
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:58,120
 Maybe God will start loving you.

107
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:01,840
 But what the gospel tells us is something completely different.

108
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:05,680
 The gospel says, God loves you when you are still unworthy.

109
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:09,560
 And this is the grace from God.

110
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:39,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

111
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:43,360
 There is another reason Paul waits until chapter 4

112
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:45,560
 to talk about Christian living.

113
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:47,320
 Paul knows this.

114
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:50,400
 It's so true that if you don't know who you are,

115
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:53,440
 you will never live the way that you are supposed to live.

116
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:55,800
 Without gospel and doctrine, what's

117
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:59,160
 left here or in Christianity?

118
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:03,120
 When you are told to try hard and better

119
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:07,560
 and become a better person, that is not gospel.

120
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:09,680
 That is moral advice.

121
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:36,440
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

122
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:39,840
 And this world always has plenty of moral advice.

123
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:42,920
 When we are in trouble, we always

124
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:46,160
 focus solely on changing the outside circumstances

125
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:49,680
 or our behavior, and we miss the root issue--

126
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:51,840
 understanding the gospel.

127
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:54,040
 Why do we become jealous?

128
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:55,440
 Why do we fight?

129
00:10:55,440 --> 00:10:57,360
 Why do we hurt each other?

130
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:59,240
 Because we forgot who we are.

131
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:03,480
 We forgot that we are the people of grace.

132
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:09,200
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

133
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:11,680
 That's why Paul waits until chapter 4

134
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:14,040
 to start talking about how we should live.

135
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:32,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

136
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:33,800
 Paul says, "You are called."

137
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:35,840
 What does that actually mean?

138
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:38,800
 It means we did not find God first by ourselves.

139
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:42,440
 God calls us first, just like Lazarus.

140
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:47,480
 Jesus stood before a dead man and said, "Lazarus, come out."

141
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:50,440
 A dead man can never respond on his own

142
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:52,840
 unless Jesus calls him.

143
00:11:52,840 --> 00:12:08,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

144
00:12:08,040 --> 00:12:23,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

145
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:26,920
 In the same way, spiritually speaking, we were dead.

146
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:28,560
 But God called us.

147
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:30,320
 So let me ask you this.

148
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:32,760
 Why are you a Christian?

149
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:36,480
 Is it because that you are smarter or better or more

150
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:38,480
 spiritual than others?

151
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:39,440
 No.

152
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:41,320
 It is about grace.

153
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:43,880
 Grace came to you.

154
00:12:43,880 --> 00:13:00,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

155
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:04,280
 When Paul says, "Walking in a manner worthy of your calling,"

156
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:06,240
 what does "worthy" mean?

157
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:08,960
 It does not mean earning salvation.

158
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:12,240
 Paul is not saying, "Behave better

159
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:14,600
 so you deserve this salvation."

160
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,720
 That's not what he means.

161
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:42,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

162
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:48,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

163
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:51,440
 So what he actually means here--

164
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:54,560
 let your life match the grace you have received.

165
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:57,560
 Live in a way that fits your identity.

166
00:13:57,560 --> 00:14:01,520
 If your identity is heavenly, don't live like the world.

167
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:04,400
 Imagine Pastor Mark got drunk every day,

168
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:07,000
 lying outside of our church building.

169
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,120
 So what would you say?

170
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:12,680
 Then you might say, that doesn't fit.

171
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:13,920
 It doesn't match.

172
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:18,240
 In the same way, God has given us a glorious identity.

173
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:21,120
 Our lives should reflect that identity.

174
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:23,760
 Next, let's look at the second point.

175
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:44,200
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

176
00:14:44,200 --> 00:15:04,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

177
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:08,440
 Verses 2 says, "With all humility and gentleness,

178
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:12,280
 with patience, bearing with one another in love."

179
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:16,400
 Before Paul talks about unity, he first talks about characters.

180
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:17,120
 Why?

181
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:19,000
 Because the biggest problem in a church

182
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,240
 is usually not the structure.

183
00:15:21,240 --> 00:15:23,840
 It is the people inside the church.

184
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:27,280
 A church may have a perfect system, a strong structure,

185
00:15:27,280 --> 00:15:29,080
 a well-organized ministry.

186
00:15:29,080 --> 00:15:32,320
 But if the people are spiritually immature,

187
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:34,200
 everything can still fall apart.

188
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:38,080
 That's why Paul starts talking about characters.

189
00:15:38,080 --> 00:16:08,000
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

190
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,520
 Paul gives us four types of characters.

191
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:12,960
 The first one, he mentioned humility.

192
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:16,520
 In Greek culture, humility was seen as weakness and not

193
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:19,000
 that good in that culture.

194
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,840
 But in scripture, humility is a character of Christ.

195
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:24,880
 Jesus is the Son of God.

196
00:16:24,880 --> 00:16:26,280
 He's the true King.

197
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:28,760
 But where was he born?

198
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:33,640
 Not in a palace, in a mansion, not into a noble family,

199
00:16:33,640 --> 00:16:36,400
 but into a home of a carpenter.

200
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:39,160
 He humbled himself and obeyed the Father,

201
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:42,520
 even to the point of death on a cross.

202
00:16:42,520 --> 00:17:04,280
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

203
00:17:04,280 --> 00:17:06,920
 So what is biblical humility?

204
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:10,040
 It's not low self-esteem.

205
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:12,960
 It's not thinking poorly of yourself.

206
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:15,600
 True humility means this.

207
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:18,560
 You are no longer centered on yourself.

208
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:20,560
 You are centered on God.

209
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:23,720
 Many conflicts in church are rooted in pride.

210
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:26,560
 Why won't the people listen to me?

211
00:17:26,560 --> 00:17:29,480
 Why won't they do the things in my way?

212
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:32,240
 Why doesn't anyone respect me?

213
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:37,720
 Pride destroys unity, and humility builds unity.

214
00:17:37,720 --> 00:18:06,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

215
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:11,560
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

216
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:13,440
 Second, gentleness.

217
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:15,360
 Gentleness is not weakness.

218
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:18,360
 Gentleness is strength under control.

219
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:19,760
 Think of a horse.

220
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:22,760
 A horse is powerful, but when trained,

221
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:26,280
 the strength is under the control of its master.

222
00:18:26,280 --> 00:18:27,880
 That is gentleness.

223
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:31,720
 Jesus said, "I am gentle and lowly in heart."

224
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:35,920
 Jesus was gentlest person who ever lived.

225
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:38,440
 And yet, he was full of power.

226
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:39,880
 He calmed storms.

227
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:41,520
 He cast out demons.

228
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:43,360
 He raised the dead.

229
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:47,480
 Gentleness does not mean having no power.

230
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:50,960
 It means having power, but not abusing it.

231
00:18:50,960 --> 00:19:07,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

232
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:24,280
 The third point is patience, and the fourth one

233
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:26,760
 is bearing with one another.

234
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:29,680
 There were always some people in the church

235
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:32,200
 that we think we might not like.

236
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:35,440
 But the same is true in the family life, too.

237
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:39,760
 Sometimes even our spouse, children, parents,

238
00:19:39,760 --> 00:19:42,760
 sometimes we have conflict moment with them.

239
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:45,280
 However, why should we be patient?

240
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:48,080
 Because Christ has been patient with us.

241
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:51,000
 We've seen against God again and again.

242
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,880
 We've failed him again and again.

243
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:55,520
 Let him disappointed.

244
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:59,680
 Yet God has shown enormous patience towards us,

245
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:02,080
 and we must treat others the same way.

246
00:20:02,080 --> 00:20:03,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

247
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:16,800
 Paul adds an important phrase, "with all."

248
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:20,160
 Not just humility, not just gentleness,

249
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:23,000
 but with all humility.

250
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:26,120
 And this means not only when life is easy,

251
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:29,120
 but in every situation, even though in the toughest

252
00:20:29,120 --> 00:20:32,400
 moment in your life, in good times, in hard times,

253
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:34,800
 when life is smooth or when life is painful.

254
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:35,800
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

255
00:20:46,800 --> 00:21:03,840
 Now, here is the real question.

256
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:08,080
 Can people actually produce these characters on their own?

257
00:21:08,080 --> 00:21:09,880
 Can we truly be humble?

258
00:21:09,880 --> 00:21:12,120
 Can we truly be gentle?

259
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:17,160
 Can we truly be patient only by our efforts?

260
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:18,280
 No.

261
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:20,520
 What comes naturally to us?

262
00:21:20,520 --> 00:21:22,880
 Protecting ourselves, defending ourselves,

263
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:25,880
 exhorting ourselves, because our nature tendency

264
00:21:25,880 --> 00:21:27,840
 is always self-centered.

265
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:28,720
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

266
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:58,120
 Paul is not saying, try hard to be a better person.

267
00:21:58,120 --> 00:22:00,000
 Improve yourself a little bit more.

268
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:01,800
 Be more disciplined.

269
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:02,680
 No.

270
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:05,480
 Paul is saying, you need the gospel.

271
00:22:05,480 --> 00:22:08,000
 When we truly understand the gospel,

272
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:11,800
 the Holy Spirit begins shaping the life of Christ in us.

273
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:15,280
 Humility and gentleness are not something we fake.

274
00:22:15,280 --> 00:22:18,360
 They are not something we force ourselves to perform.

275
00:22:18,360 --> 00:22:21,040
 They are the fruit of spirit.

276
00:22:21,040 --> 00:22:40,800
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

277
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:43,500
 Only when you understand what the gospel can,

278
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:47,480
 you can become truly humble.

279
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:49,120
 Only when you understand the gospel

280
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:51,000
 can you become truly gentle.

281
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:53,160
 And only when you understand the gospel

282
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:56,760
 can you preserve the true unity.

283
00:22:56,760 --> 00:23:00,400
 Apart from the gospel, there is no real humility,

284
00:23:00,400 --> 00:23:04,000
 no real gentleness, and no real unity.

285
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:26,640
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

286
00:23:26,640 --> 00:23:29,440
 And even more than that, those four characters

287
00:23:29,440 --> 00:23:31,360
 describe Jesus himself.

288
00:23:31,360 --> 00:23:34,880
 Jesus is humble, Jesus is gentle, he is patient,

289
00:23:34,880 --> 00:23:36,520
 Jesus is gracious.

290
00:23:36,520 --> 00:23:39,880
 The Christian life is about reflecting Christ

291
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:42,840
 like the moon reflects the light of the sun.

292
00:23:42,840 --> 00:23:46,120
 Our lives are meant to reflect Christ.

293
00:23:46,120 --> 00:24:16,040
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

294
00:24:16,040 --> 00:24:18,920
 Paul emphasized unity here.

295
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:20,960
 Why is unity so important?

296
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:23,240
 Because God is the God of unity.

297
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:26,400
 God's plan is that in the fullness of time,

298
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:29,440
 all things will be united in Christ.

299
00:24:29,440 --> 00:24:32,640
 And the goal of salvation is reconciliation.

300
00:24:32,640 --> 00:24:35,480
 Reconciliation between God and man,

301
00:24:35,480 --> 00:24:38,600
 the reconciliation among people.

302
00:24:38,600 --> 00:24:41,000
 Sin always works against unity.

303
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:44,200
 Sin brings division, conflict, hostility,

304
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:47,240
 and broken relationship.

305
00:24:47,240 --> 00:24:59,240
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

306
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:00,280
 Notice Paul's word.

307
00:25:00,280 --> 00:25:02,800
 He does not say create unity.

308
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:04,800
 He says maintain unity.

309
00:25:04,800 --> 00:25:05,640
 Why?

310
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:09,480
 Because true unity is not something that we can create.

311
00:25:09,480 --> 00:25:13,080
 It is something the Holy Spirit has already given.

312
00:25:13,080 --> 00:25:29,480
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

313
00:25:29,480 --> 00:25:32,280
 Christ has always torn down the division war

314
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:34,480
 through his death on cross.

315
00:25:34,480 --> 00:25:37,640
 The problem is not that church has no unity.

316
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:39,320
 The real problem is that we often

317
00:25:39,320 --> 00:25:43,120
 destroy the unity God has already given us.

318
00:25:43,120 --> 00:25:44,840
 How do we destroy it?

319
00:25:44,840 --> 00:25:49,040
 By our pride, bitterness, judgment, conflict,

320
00:25:49,040 --> 00:25:50,400
 and division.

321
00:25:50,400 --> 00:26:01,560
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

322
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:05,680
 That is why Paul says we must be eager to maintain unity.

323
00:26:05,680 --> 00:26:07,480
 What does eager mean?

324
00:26:07,480 --> 00:26:10,120
 It means unity does not come easy.

325
00:26:10,120 --> 00:26:11,560
 It costs something.

326
00:26:11,560 --> 00:26:13,640
 We must lay down ourselves.

327
00:26:13,640 --> 00:26:15,280
 We must forgive.

328
00:26:15,280 --> 00:26:17,200
 We must be patient.

329
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:47,160
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

330
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:51,080
 The foundation of church unity is not human effort.

331
00:26:51,080 --> 00:26:55,320
 The foundation is unity of triune God.

332
00:26:55,320 --> 00:26:57,600
 One body, one spirit.

333
00:26:57,600 --> 00:27:02,600
 This points to the Holy Spirit who makes the church one body.

334
00:27:02,600 --> 00:27:05,880
 One Lord, one faith, one baptism.

335
00:27:05,880 --> 00:27:08,040
 This point to Christ.

336
00:27:08,040 --> 00:27:12,560
 We belong to the same Lord, one God and Father.

337
00:27:12,560 --> 00:27:14,720
 This points to the Father.

338
00:27:14,720 --> 00:27:17,200
 We share the same Heavenly Father.

339
00:27:17,200 --> 00:27:21,600
 The Father, the Son, and the Holy Spirit are not divided.

340
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:23,800
 They are perfectly united.

341
00:27:23,800 --> 00:27:27,880
 That is why the church must be united.

342
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:44,360
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

343
00:27:44,360 --> 00:27:47,000
 What does Satan love to see the most?

344
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:50,560
 Not church closing, not Sunday worship stopping.

345
00:27:50,560 --> 00:27:54,440
 What Satan loves most is this.

346
00:27:54,440 --> 00:27:56,240
 Church still gathers.

347
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:58,600
 The song are still singing.

348
00:27:58,600 --> 00:28:00,440
 The sermon still preached.

349
00:28:00,440 --> 00:28:03,560
 But brothers and sisters become cold to each other.

350
00:28:03,560 --> 00:28:06,160
 They attack one another, judge one another,

351
00:28:06,160 --> 00:28:07,400
 hurt one another.

352
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:10,600
 That destroyed the witness of the church.

353
00:28:10,600 --> 00:28:40,000
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

354
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:45,520
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

355
00:28:45,520 --> 00:28:49,200
 But then verse 7 says, grace was given to each one of us

356
00:28:49,200 --> 00:28:52,080
 according to the measure of Christ's gift.

357
00:28:52,080 --> 00:28:53,480
 What does that mean?

358
00:28:53,480 --> 00:28:56,560
 Unity does not mean uniformity.

359
00:28:56,560 --> 00:28:59,400
 God does not mass produce people.

360
00:28:59,400 --> 00:29:03,920
 And the body is not made up of only eyes.

361
00:29:03,920 --> 00:29:08,680
 Or the body is not made up of only with a lot of pair of hands.

362
00:29:08,680 --> 00:29:10,400
 Every person is different.

363
00:29:10,400 --> 00:29:12,440
 Each person has different gifts.

364
00:29:12,440 --> 00:29:14,160
 Some are gifted in teaching.

365
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:17,200
 Some are gifted in caring for people.

366
00:29:17,200 --> 00:29:18,400
 Some in serving.

367
00:29:18,400 --> 00:29:19,560
 Some in leading.

368
00:29:19,560 --> 00:29:22,400
 Unity does not erase differences.

369
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:28,280
 A healthy church is united in truth and diverse in gifts.

370
00:29:28,280 --> 00:29:50,640
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

371
00:29:50,640 --> 00:29:53,200
 Brothers and sisters, the real question

372
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:56,120
 is not whether we attend church today.

373
00:29:56,120 --> 00:29:59,680
 The real question is, do we look like Christ?

374
00:29:59,680 --> 00:30:02,280
 Can your family see Christ in you?

375
00:30:02,280 --> 00:30:04,560
 Can your children see Christ in you?

376
00:30:04,560 --> 00:30:08,680
 Can your brothers and sisters see Christ in you?

377
00:30:08,680 --> 00:30:25,080
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

378
00:30:25,080 --> 00:30:29,840
 Are you building up the church or trying to tear it down?

379
00:30:29,840 --> 00:30:34,680
 Are you bringing peace or creating division?

380
00:30:34,680 --> 00:30:36,720
 May God have mercy on us.

381
00:30:36,720 --> 00:30:38,240
 May God renew us.

382
00:30:38,240 --> 00:30:41,440
 May God help us walk in manner worthy of the calling

383
00:30:41,440 --> 00:30:43,360
 we have received.

384
00:30:43,360 --> 00:30:55,680
 [NON-ENGLISH SPEECH]

385
00:30:55,680 --> 00:31:25,240
 Heavenly Father, we thank you for calling us out of darkness

386
00:31:25,240 --> 00:31:31,000
 into your marvelous light and from death into life.

387
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:34,880
 Thank you for giving us a new identity in Christ.

388
00:31:34,880 --> 00:31:38,080
 You have given us such a glorious calling,

389
00:31:38,080 --> 00:31:40,880
 and we ask you would help us live

390
00:31:40,880 --> 00:31:44,480
 lives worthy of the calling.

391
00:31:44,480 --> 00:31:48,560
 Lord, give us hearts of humility, gentleness,

392
00:31:48,560 --> 00:31:50,000
 and patience.

393
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:54,360
 Help us to reflect the character of Christ in our daily lives.

394
00:31:54,360 --> 00:31:59,200
 Teach us to love one another, bear with one another,

395
00:31:59,200 --> 00:32:02,600
 and preserve the unity of the church.

396
00:32:02,600 --> 00:32:05,760
 In Jesus' name, amen.

